{"accepted": null, "attempt": 0, "campaign_id": "pat-19-x3screen-1", "campaign_sha256": "95b7a0717ecfcc28b6595e4a88dee108d158ff7d85dddc84f7d1c56de8d5fd1d", "cloud_executions": 0, "cloud_sessions": [], "dry_run": false, "envelope_sha256": "d3eaf1de26eb36e5e0b6740391923a67f4b87f2025895fe19329c2f8aa86c8a8", "exploration": {"bundle_modified": false, "refusal": null, "report": {"files": ["plugins/foundry/tooling/foundry/trackers/linear.py", "plugins/foundry/tests/test_linear_tracker.py", "plugins/foundry/docs/linear-tracker.md"], "functions": [{"file": "plugins/foundry/tooling/foundry/trackers/linear.py", "name": "LinearTracker._validate_adr_graph"}, {"file": "plugins/foundry/tooling/foundry/trackers/linear.py", "name": "LinearTracker.import_adr_batch"}], "rationale": "The bug is in _validate_adr_graph (linear.py:~2471): when a reciprocal comment is missing (reciprocal is None) and it is in pending_comments, the code silently continues, causing replay to recreate externally-deleted comments. The fix adds an existing_documents parameter to _validate_adr_graph so that when a comment is missing, it checks whether the corresponding version-0 Document (identified by _adr_document_id(project_id, adr_id, 0)) already exists in the document store. If the Document exists, the comment was already materialized by a previous batch \u2014 its external deletion must be refused. If no Document exists, the batch never completed, so creating the comment is safe. import_adr_batch passes its by_id mapping to _validate_adr_graph to enable this check. A new test in test_linear_tracker.py covers the scenario: complete a batch, delete the reciprocal comment from the fake transport, replay, and assert TrackerConflictError with zero DocumentCreate/CommentCreate effects. linear-tracker.md is updated to document the refusal behavior."}, "report_source": "final_message", "score": {"counts": {"correct_files": 3, "counted_functions": 2, "found_files": 1, "found_functions": 1, "reported_files": 3, "tru